 "notes": "Single map sheet read from OCR (page 1). Map symbol recorded only where on the same line as the unit name (QPw); other symbols (QPph, QPmf, QPmt, Taf, Qcb...) are scattered in the OCR and were not tied to units. The Water unit was not recorded. Legend-only features (contact, drill-hole symbol) were not recorded as values. The Penholoway Formation description is printed out of order in the OCR; only legible parts were recorded and its color list was skipped. One thickness printed with '|' for a digit is read as 1, flagged inferred and sent to review.\nSUBSURFACE: cross section A-A' (page 1) is recorded with its vertical exaggeration and datum, but its unit labels (me, Qcb, Taf, QPmf, QPmt, QPw, QPph, QHfw) are scattered rows with no readable distances, and its end points, length and elevation scale (160/120/80/40 ft labels) can't be tied to positions, so no units along it were recorded. The Penholoway Formation's 'uppermost elevation of 80 feet' is not tied to a place and was kept in its description rather than as a surface. An SCGS drill-hole label appears on the map face (25-093); logs are on file at the SCGS and not in this document. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum; topographic contour interval 10 feet on the 1978 base map (page 1).",
